      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x6201" vislevel="1" flags="0xC">
    <title>INFERRED_RPM_Limiter_Offset_Decay_Step</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.46 CODE-DERIVED] A3B4 is subtracted from FF84EC by handler_RPM_Limiter. FF84EC is an RPM-count offset added into the RPM threshold path and compared in the FF8334 Engine_RPM byte domain. Therefore A3B4 is an RPM-count decay step. Q28G raw=1 -&gt; 40 RPM per handler update.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="15" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xa3b4" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>RPM/update</units>
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <rangehigh>10200</rangehigh>
    <rangelow>0</rangelow>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X * 40">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x6202" vislevel="1" flags="0xC">
    <title>INFERRED_RPM_Limiter_Ignition_Retard_Update_Delay</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.46 CODE-DERIVED] A3B5 reloads FF84F1. FF84F1 is decremented once per limiter-handler pass; when it reaches zero the limiter retard accumulator FF84F0 is stepped. Unit is controller/handler cycles, not milliseconds. Q28G raw=15.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="15" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xa3b5" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>handler cycles</units>
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <rangehigh>255</rangehigh>
    <rangelow>0</rangelow>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x6203" vislevel="1" flags="0xC">
    <title>INFERRED_RPM_Limiter_Max_Ignition_Retard</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.46 CODE-DERIVED] A3B6 caps FF84F0. FF84F0 is subtracted directly from the ignition-angle byte in set_Engine_Timing_Advance, so one count equals the ignition domain step of 0.75 deg. Q28G stock raw=0, so this ramped retard contribution is stock-disabled.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="15" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xa3b6" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>deg retard</units>
    <decimalpl>2</decimalpl>
    <rangehigh>191.25</rangehigh>
    <rangelow>0</rangelow>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X * 0.75">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x6204" vislevel="1" flags="0xC">
    <title>INFERRED_Engine_Protection_Limiter_RPM_Threshold</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.46 CODE-DERIVED] set_Engine_Limiter compares FF8334 Engine_RPM directly with A488 before entering the protection counter logic. Q28G raw=113 -&gt; 4520 RPM. Exact OEM feature name is unknown.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="15" />
