  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xEF03" flags="0x0">
    <title>EXPERT_Misfire_Channel_Scaling_Correction_Vector_Q14</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.68 STRUCTURED VECTOR / CODE-DERIVED / EXPERT] Four signed bytes at 0x831C..0x831F are indexed through the runtime channel permutation table 0x14AAC = [0,2,3,1] in the misfire path. Each selected byte is sign-extended, multiplied by the current internal word and shifted right 14, then added back to that word. Thus each element is a signed Q14 fractional correction. Q28G stock is 0,0,0,0. This is diagnostic/misfire processing, not normal engine tuning.</description>
