  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xEF08">
    <title>EXPERT_Lambda_Adaptation_Apply_Multiplicative_Learned_Trim</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.69 MASK-PRESERVING FLAG / CODE-DERIVED / EXPERT] Bit0 of calibration byte 0x85C5. In PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_01C346, when SET the learned multiplicative trim word at runtime 0xFF97F0 is multiplied into the fuel/lambda path with Q15 scaling. Stock 0x85C5=0x03, so bit0 is SET. Editing this flag changes only mask 0x01 and preserves all other bits. Expert adaptation control; preserve stock unless intentionally testing learned-trim behavior.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="18" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x85c5" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x01</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xEF09">
    <title>EXPERT_Lambda_Adaptation_Apply_Additive_Learned_Trim</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.69 MASK-PRESERVING FLAG / CODE-DERIVED / EXPERT] Bit1 of calibration byte 0x85C5. In PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_01C346, when SET the signed learned additive trim at runtime 0xFF8514 is conditionally added to the fuel/lambda path. Stock 0x85C5=0x03, so bit1 is SET. Editing this flag changes only mask 0x02 and preserves all other bits. Expert adaptation control.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="18" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x85c5" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x02</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xEF0A">
    <title>EXPERT_Lambda_Adaptation_Helper_Path_Enable</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.69 MASK-PRESERVING FLAG / CODE-DERIVED / EXPERT] Bit7 of calibration byte 0x85C5. In PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_01DE0E, when SET this bit invokes the lambda-adaptation helper path at 0x0001DD7C. Stock 0x85C5=0x03, so bit7 is CLEAR. The same routine also tests the whole byte for nonzero before broader adaptation processing; therefore this flag is expert-only and should normally remain stock. Editing changes only mask 0x80.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="18" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x85c5" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x80</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
</XDFFORMAT>